1. Create a Figma Design file and add a 1440 x 1024 frame named Cellular_System.
2. Draw a seven-cell hexagonal cluster using the Polygon tool (6 sides); label the cells 1 to 7.
3. Place a BTS tower icon at the centre of every cell and a mobile station icon in one cell.
4. Draw BSC, MSC, HLR/VLR and PSTN as rounded rectangles and convert each to a component.
5. Connect the blocks with lines (dashed for the radio link Um, solid for wired Abis and A interfaces) and label the interfaces.
6. Create an Info Card component with two variants, Hidden and Visible, holding the block name and its function.
7. In Prototype mode set On click on each block to Change to the Visible variant, and On click on the card to return to Hidden.
8. Press Present and test every block.
